<section class="why-local">

  <div class="container why-grid">

    <div class="why-content">

      <span class="overline">
        WHY LOCAL MATTERS
      </span>

      <h2>
        Why We Do Not
        <span>Just Cover a Radius</span>
      </h2>

      <p>
        Most of the winter, heating systems in this county coast. Our
        winters are mild and wet, and a furnace that is quietly failing
        can go unnoticed for months.
      </p>

      <p>
        Then the wind swings around and comes down out of the Fraser
        Canyon from the northeast. The temperature drops hard for a few
        days, every heating system in Whatcom County gets asked to work
        properly for the first time all season, and the marginal ones
        give up.
      </p>

      <p>
        That is when we get busy, and it happens county wide at the same
        time rather than neighbourhood by neighbourhood.
      </p>

      <p>
        Knowing that pattern is the difference between a service area and
        a service map. It is why we push maintenance in September rather
        than December, and why we keep ignition parts stocked deeper than
        a mild climate would suggest we need to.
      </p>

    </div>

    <div class="why-image">

      <img
        src="/images/areas-hub-hero.webp"
        alt="Heating service across Whatcom County"
      />

    </div>

  </div>

</section>

